{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789914316,"nonce":"pDHPhrcpPTCLaVc8nIcGCFOLP10=","title":"LICM hoisted a load past a store through another copy of the same pointer","message":"The per-Load alias check takes two distinct SSA roots for distinct\nmemory. Two roots that are both loads of one pointer slot name one\nobject: a list's element pointer is read from its header wherever it is\nneeded, so a loop that stores `mt[i]` through one read of the pointer\nand reads `mt[623]` through another had the read hoisted out, and the\nMersenne Twister's init_by_array wrapped the state with a stale word.\n\nThe same rule broke inside an outlined resume point (e2314a6e): the\nregion's parameters are the values the body had live at its header,\namong them a pointer to the buffer and a pointer 623 words into it,\nwhich as two parameters looked like distinct objects. The seed of\nrandom.seed re-run after the first call, whose frame had left into the\nregion, produced a different sequence (0.3957 where CPython gives\n0.8444), and only when the request was served inline or the worker was\nquick enough, so the first draws were right one run in two.\n\nFix: a load of a pointer from an address already loaded from resolves\nto the first such load; a parameter of an outlined region may alias any\nother root. Regression tests in licm.rs.","files":null}]}